# Presents (data/gifts.json, Gifts): one every 3 h of wall clock into a pocket of 3, from when the
# boxes tab opens (pile_full has it, so the clock starts on load). Your pet holds one in its paws on
# the home tab; tap: shake, pop, the box flies to the pile (a toy capsule shows its card). Out on your
# windows it digs one up on a window edge and wears it on its head until you tap it.
from pile_full
paws everything              # the profile keeps its settings between runs
task none                    # your pet sits on its spot (the pile holds still)
view full
tab home
wait 1
expect fits
expect gifts 0
gift-clock 2.9
expect gifts 0               # not yet: 3 h a present
gift-clock 0.2
expect gifts 1
wait 1
shot home_present
gift-clock 20
expect gifts 3               # the pocket holds 3, however long it's been
wait 1
shot home_three
expect fits
expect pile starter 30
gift-roll one
home gift
shot home_shake
shot home_pop
wait 1
expect gifts 2
expect pile starter 31
shot home_opened
gift-roll toy
home gift
wait 1
shot home_toy
expect gifts 1
expect pile starter 32
expect fits
wait popup                   # your first toy opens the workbench: its card waits for the toy's
click "lovely*"
task none
gift 2
desk on                       # it drops in, lands on the window and digs straight away
wait dig
wait 0.6
shot desk_dig
wait worn
wait 1
shot desk_worn
desk good
wait 1
shot desk_hold                # a good pull held up over the present on its head
wait 4
gift-roll two
desk tap
shot desk_pop
expect gifts 1
expect pile starter 34
wait 2
shot desk_after               # no dig for a while after a tap
paws off
gift 1
wait 3
shot desk_off                 # off: no digging, the present waits on the home tab
desk off
paws everything
expect fits
view full
tab home
task boxes                   # busy with the pile: the present waits on the floor by its spot
gift 3
wait 4
shot home_busy
wait 3
shot home_busy_rest           # still on the floor while it rests between packs
task none
expect fits
